        <div id="what-is-kinomap" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What Is Kinomap, and Why Use It on a Treadmill?</h2>
<p>
            Kinomap is a training app for treadmills, bikes, rowers and ellipticals. Its best-known
            feature is a library of real-world route videos filmed by its users and partners: you walk
            or run on the treadmill while the video plays at a pace that follows yours. It also offers
            structured workouts, multiplayer sessions and training plans. It runs on a phone, tablet,
            computer or smart TV rather than on the treadmill&rsquo;s own screen, which is why a
            treadmill with a simple LCD console can use it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The appeal on a treadmill is variety without lock-in. iFIT, Peloton and JRNY only run on their
            own brands&rsquo; machines, and those machines tend to cost more. Kinomap works on any
            treadmill that can share its data over Bluetooth in a way the app understands, and you can
            cancel it and keep the treadmill fully working. Kinomap is a subscription service with a
            free tier and a paid tier; check its current prices and what the free tier includes on the
            Kinomap site rather than relying on any figure you have seen quoted.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">App</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Works on</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Main draw</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Kinomap</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Many Bluetooth treadmills from different brands</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Real-world route videos, workouts</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Zwift</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Bluetooth treadmills, or any treadmill with a foot pod</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Animated virtual worlds, group runs</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">FitShow</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmills built with FitShow-compatible consoles</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Basic tracking and control</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">iFIT</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">NordicTrack and ProForm</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Trainer-led classes that control the machine</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Peloton</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Peloton Tread; the app also works with any treadmill for classes</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Studio classes</td></tr>
