              They do different things. Kinomap's main draw is real-world route videos; Zwift's is animated virtual worlds and group runs. Several treadmills here name both, so you can try each. Zwift also works with a foot pod on treadmills that cannot connect directly.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can I use Kinomap on a NordicTrack treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack treadmills are built around iFIT, and their listings do not name Kinomap. If you want Kinomap, buy a treadmill whose listing or Kinomap's equipment list names it.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

